  "Number": 26,
  "Question": "For any real value of \\(x\\) the maximum value of \\(8x-3x^2\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac83\\)",
    "C": "\\(4\\)",
    "D": "\\(5\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{16}{3}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "A real square is nonnegative, so writing the expression as a constant minus a square will reveal its maximum. Completing the square gives\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n8x-3x^2\n&=-3\\left[\\left(x-\\frac43\\right)^2-\\frac{16}{9}\\right]\\\\\n&=\\frac{16}{3}-3\\left(x-\\frac43\\right)^2.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe subtracted term is nonnegative for every real \\(x\\), so the expression is at most \\(\\frac{16}{3}\\). Equality occurs when \\(x=\\frac43\\), making this bound attainable. The maximum is therefore \\(\\frac{16}{3}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
